Package: aurora-sep
Architecture: all
Depends: aurora-touchid-rearm,
 aurora-xart,
 fprintd-aurora (>= 1.94.5-4+aurora1),
 keyutils,
 kmod,
 libfprint-aurora (>= 1:1.94.100-1+aurora1),
 libpam-fprintd (>= 1.94.5-4+aurora1),
 python3,
 systemd,
 ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: libglib2.0-bin
Description: SEP trusted-key and Touch ID integration for Aurora
 Loads the apple_sep Secure Enclave driver after persistent storage is
 mounted and verifies trusted key sealing and unsealing. On machines with a
 fingerprint reader it also sets up the per-device calibration, activates
 Touch ID before fprintd starts and lets fprintd use the Aurora libfprint
 driver. Touch ID is reported ready only when the sensor attached, the
 fingerprints were restored and a match can save its state. Initialization
 runs in the background without holding up the desktop.
 .
 A fingerprint or the password unlocks the lock screen and answers sudo and
 polkit; the login screen, the console login, su and ssh ask for the
 password. A short press of the power button, which is the Touch ID sensor,
 suspends.
